  <h2 id="research-associate">Research associate and JRF pay: the research runway</h2>

  <p>
    "Research associate" and "JRF" get used almost interchangeably by students, but they are financially very different things.
  </p>

  <p>
    An industry research associate is an actual salaried job. A JRF (Junior Research Fellowship) is a government stipend for pursuing a funded PhD - it is a runway, not a career salary.
  </p>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table">
