    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take</p>
    <p>
      A JRF stipend is designed to cover a researcher's living costs during a PhD, not to be compared against an industry salary. Treat the roughly Rs 37,000-42,000 a month figure as your budget for several years, not as evidence that research pays badly - the real comparison is the post-PhD scientist salary against the years and opportunity cost it took to get there.
    </p>
    <p>
      If pure lab research does not excite you enough to sustain that runway, an industry research-associate role or a pivot toward quality, regulatory, or bioinformatics work reaches a comparable or better salary faster.
    </p>
  </div>

