  <h2 id="sources">How these numbers were built</h2>

  <p>
    Every range in this guide was cross-checked across current salary-tracking platforms - including AmbitionBox, Payscale, Glassdoor, and Indeed - plus official government and institutional pay references: the 7th Central Pay Commission pay matrix, ICAR/ASRB recruitment notifications, CSIR's published scientist pay structure, the UGC 7th CPC academic pay scale, and the Regional Centre for Biotechnology's DBT-Research Associateship programme page. City-wise and named-employer figures (Bengaluru, Hyderabad, Pune, Delhi-NCR, Biocon, Syngene, Serum Institute of India, and Dr. Reddy's Laboratories) were checked against each company's own AmbitionBox and Glassdoor India salary pages rather than a generic national average alone.
  </p>

  <p>
    These platforms and sources disagree with each other, sometimes by a wide margin, because they draw on different sample sizes, self-reported figures, cities, employer mixes, and years of data. Fellowship amounts in particular get revised periodically by the notifying body.
  </p>

  <p class="note-line">
    Treat every figure in this article as a planning range, not a guaranteed offer. Verify current openings, city-specific pay, and the latest fellowship or pay-matrix notification before making a financial commitment based on any single number - including the ones here.
  </p>

